# Fixed 2026-09-29, defect 131's class, lane X4. Symptom: a record's fields
# in braces with the `{` alone on the line below the head, Allman's style,
# cost `expected the end of the line after record P` with its caret on the
# `{`, on the line after the one it named, which had ended (lane X1's finding
# 12): a caret stands on the line whose mistake it names. And the fields
# inside went unread, their mistakes unsaid; a variant and an `extern` group
# the same. Cause: a `{` below the head was taken for the head's junk
# wherever it stood. A `{` alone on the line below a head whose line ended,
# past blank and comment lines, is now told where it stands in the words of
# the head's own report where no members are indented below it,
# `empty_record`, `empty_variant` or `expected_extern_block`, saying where the
# members go; and the members inside are read. Over junk on the head's line
# the junk is told on that line, and the `{` below on its own.

record P
{  #~ empty_record
    x: i64
    y i64  #~ expected_field_type
}

variant C
{  #~ empty_variant
    red
    5  #~ expected_case
}

extern "m.h"
{  #~ expected_extern_block
    function q(x i64) -> i64  #~ expected_parameter_type
}

record Q )  #~ expected_end_of_line
{  #~ empty_record
    z: i64
}

record R

# the fields of R
{  #~ empty_record
    w: i64
}

function main()
    print(1)
